FILES MODIFIED:
- web/package.json - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- web/package-lock.json - Updated with new dependency and its sub-dependencies
- web/src/app/(en)/layout.tsx - Added Analytics import and component for English locale
- web/src/app/pt/layout.tsx - Added Analytics import and component for Portuguese locale

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS:
Following the official Vercel documentation, I:

1. Installed the @vercel/analytics package version 2.0.1
2. Added the Analytics component import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
3. Placed the <Analytics /> component inside the <body> tag in both layout files
4. This approach works for the Next.js App Router architecture with multiple localized layouts

The project has two root layouts:
- (en)/layout.tsx for the English version
- pt/layout.tsx for the Portuguese version

Both layouts now include the Analytics component, ensuring tracking works across all language versions.

NEXT STEPS FOR DEPLOYMENT:
According to Vercel documentation, to enable analytics:
1. Navigate to your Vercel project's Analytics section in the dashboard
2. Click the "Enable" button to activate Web Analytics
3. Deploy the changes using `vercel deploy` or through git integration
4. Verify tracking is active by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

